The bug was caused by the logic in `CoordActionInputCheckXCommand` that incorrectly handled the condition for queuing a timeout command when there were unresolved dependencies. Specifically, it relied on the existence of non-existent input files, which could lead to a scenario where the timeout command was not queued even when it should have been, allowing coordinator jobs with unresolved dependencies to continue running indefinitely instead of timing out.

